Confidential Helpline: This provides a confidential service to support staff who are experiencing unacceptable behaviours. To contact the TUBU Helpline, call 0300 131 0052, Monday-Friday, 9am-5pm (excluding Bank Holidays);

Mediation: This service seeks to resolve workplace conflict. Further information, including how to access the service, can be found on the mediation pages on the Intranet;

Climate Assessments: These assess the climate at individual prisons by looking at the lived experiences of staff (i.e. the perceptions and attitudes) to identify any issues within those prisons;

Investigations: TUBU provides a specialist investigation service to enable managers to access trained investigators with expertise in bullying, harassment and discrimination cases, and/or advice or signposting for more complex and sensitive cases;

Unacceptable Behaviour Change Programme: TUBU provides a programme of awareness sessions to increase understanding of how to recognise, report, and address unacceptable behaviour and create environments where it feels safe to speak up if something is not right.

